── detail · template ──
AS YOU TYPE
✓ mentions the group picked under user group (in the review channel); posts: Review please <!subteam^S0REVIEW01>: <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263|mr> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard

The message: {mrs} is the merge request linked with its words, or one bullet each for several; {group} mentions the user group picked above, and {@handle} any of Slack's user groups by its handle. Both are sent as Slack's mention of the group's id, so it pings, and only in the review channel. :name: is an emoji.

ACCEPTS
text with {mrs}; {group} and {@handle} optional

NOW
{group} :gitlab: {mrs}

WITH A SAMPLE MERGE REQUEST
Review please @review-squad: mr <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard

WITH TWO
Review please @review-squad:
• api !263 <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard
• web !12 <https://git.example/acme/team-a/web/-/merge_requests/12> Show the stats

